    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, there is only a configuration option for defining an `active()` function to customize the whole statusline.\nI would like to use a mechanism to just override section functions, like `section_location()`.\n\nThe following code shows my hack to modify the location display:\n\n```lua\nlocal MiniStatusline = require(\"mini.statusline\")\n---@diagnostic disable-next-line: duplicate-set-field\nMiniStatusline.section_location = function(args)\n\t-- see ~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/statusline.lua:424\n\tif MiniStatusline.is_truncated(args.trunc_width) then\n\t\treturn \"%l|%2v\"\n\telse\n\t\treturn '%l/%L│%2v/%-2{virtcol(\"$\") - 1}'\n\tend\nend\nMiniStatusline.setup()\n```\n\nDefault:\n<img width=\"368\" height=\"19\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b891940c-65c7-4884-ba36-d0ae1ced09a3\" />\n\nMy config (`/` instead of `|`):\n<img width=\"368\" height=\"19\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3144140a-46d0-4697-8aaa-41dd9dfdb5ef\" />",
