        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThis strict separation of how to adjust the statusline content is intentional: either use default content or have a maximum flexibility by writing a custom content function. It is done to manage complexity of the module, as statuslines are something that tend to have a big range of customization preferences.\n\nThere is an [example of default content](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-statusline.html#ministatusline-example-content-defaultcontent) that can be used as a starter. Replacing the `local location = ...` line with something that you prefer better is the suggested approach here.",
